     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant 0248: 89% of contracts awarded and 89% disbursed as of 17 Jun 2022</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Progress Toward Outcome: The government PCR indicates IRR of 15% by 2019 for agribusinesses awarded in 2013. For the HIMALI subprojects as a whole, an IRR of 20% is forecasted by 2022. This will be further analyzed during the preparation of the PCR by ADB.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Social Monitoring Reports | Jul 2018: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/37292/37292-042-smr-en_0.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: Output 1.

640 agribusinesses subprojects partially financed by the Project, of which 53 are to farmer groups (including 28 cooperatives), and 124 (19%) to women-led agribusinesses. Of the total, 172 (27%) are medium-sized and 20 (3%) are large-sized (6 women-led) and the remaining 453 are small sized agribusinesses.

Two abbatoirs were supported; 6.63 km of pasture trails upgraded in Rasuwa district; Additionally, 32 different tracks to pasture lands in Dolpa, Humla, Jumla, and Sankhuwasabha were also improved.

Output 2:

A total of 4,991 persons received value chain training; 6,353 persons completed business plan preparation training; 608 persons completed agribusiness management training. Women&apos;s participation is 32.5% overall.

Towards strengthening of Ministry of Agriculture and Livestock extension offices, 79 civil works packages were financed to build new infrastructure or rehabilitate existing facilities of District Agriculture Development Offices, District Livestock Services Offices, and research centers.

Output 3:

Project was successfully implemented with effective grievance redress mechanisms in place.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
